# THE KAIZO ASSET OVERLAY IS PUBLISH-GATED. Nothing in here is committed.
#
# `sprites/` holds two kinds of art (each entry in manifest.json records
# which, as `source`):
#
#   source: "vanilla" — extracted from the player's own unmodified data.win.
#           The standing asset policy already clears vanilla sprites to ship;
#           they are held back only because they arrive alongside the gated
#           art and separating them is a deliberate decision, not a default.
#
#   source: "mod"     — EnderCat8's own art for Kaizo Roaring Knight.
#           kaizo/HANDOFF.md §5-C: recreating and publishing another author's
#           work needs their permission. Until that is given, this must not
#           reach a public repo.
#
# The repo-root .gitignore already blocks `*.png` everywhere except
# `assets/sprites/`, so the frames were covered. manifest.json and masks.json
# were NOT — and masks.json carries collision geometry derived from the
# gated art. This file closes that hole explicitly rather than relying on a
# rule written for a different purpose.
#
# Regenerate any time with: node kaizo/tools/pack-kaizo-sprites.mjs
*
# ...except this file. A bare `*` ignores the .gitignore too, so the gate
# would vanish from a fresh clone — leaving the next session to re-derive it
# from scratch, which is exactly how a gate gets lost.
!.gitignore
